course: dictionary
lesson: 11279
title: A wristwatch in a Roman film
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wristwatch is a small clock you wear on a strap or band around your wrist. You read the time on it in maths lessons, either from hands, like a clock on the wall (analogue), or from numbers (digital).
explain: Sophie in Bristol watches a Roman film and says, «Gurt lush, but why's the centurion wearing a wristwatch?» Gurt is West Country for very, and lush means lovely. Sophie knows wristwatches did not exist in Roman times, so the wristwatch looks wrong to her.
explain: Something that belongs to the wrong time is called an anachronism. A Roman soldier with a wristwatch is one, and so is a Viking with a smartphone. Spotting them is a good way to think about when things were really used.
fact: A wristwatch is a small clock worn on a strap or band around your wrist.
fact: Wristwatches became common about a hundred years ago; before that, people carried pocket watches.
fact: A smartwatch is a kind of wristwatch.
fact: An anachronism is something that belongs to another time, such as a Roman soldier with a wristwatch.
fact: «Gurt» (West Country) means very; «lush» means lovely.
exercise: What is a wristwatch? | *A small clock you wear on a strap around your wrist | A bracelet with no clock inside | A pocket for coins | A large clock that hangs on a wall
exercise: In a maths lesson, what might you read on a wristwatch? | The name of a city | *The time | A map of the world | The weather forecast
exercise: Which of these is a kind of wristwatch? | *A smartwatch | A sundial | A pocket watch | A wall clock
test: Before wristwatches became common, what did many people carry instead? | A smartphone | A clock on a wall | *A pocket watch | A bracelet
test: In «Gurt lush, but why's the centurion wearing a wristwatch?», what is wrong? | Lush means dirty | Centurions never wore any jewellery at all | Gurt means small, so the sentence is wrong | *A wristwatch belongs to a later time than Roman soldiers, so it is an anachronism
exam: Which best describes an anachronism? | A word that means very old | A kind of smartwatch with a screen | *Something that belongs to another time, such as a Roman soldier with a wristwatch | A small clock worn on the wrist
